--- contracts
$ sh main/tracker-read.sh --help
    usage: sh tracker-read.sh --url URL
    
    Prints one GitHub or GitLab issue as markdown. Use it when the human points
    at an issue link to read; to keep it in an effort's context, use
    context-add-issue.sh.
    
    Options:
      --url URL  the issue link: host github.com only, path /OWNER/REPO/issues/N;
                 or GitLab: any host without a port, path ending /-/issues/N
    Requires:  gh or glab logged in for the link's host, the issue visible to it
    Writes:    nothing
    Stdout:    the issue: title, link, state, author, date, body, then comments
               oldest first (GitLab: the first 100), at most 500 lines; the line
               "## Comments not read (REASON)" replaces comments it can't read;
               nothing on any other exit
    Exit:
      0  read; when cut, stderr gets "tracker-read.sh: truncated: showing 500
         of N lines"
      1  the read failed or a tracker call timed out after 30 s; the reason is
         on stderr
      2  refused, nothing changed; the reason is on stderr
      3  not an issue link (pull or merge request, Jira, other): read it as any
         other link
    [exit 0]
$ sh main/context-add-issue.sh --help
    usage: sh context-add-issue.sh --effort FOLDER --url URL
    
    Copies one GitHub or GitLab issue into the open effort's context draft, so
    the next context cut includes it.
    
    Options:
      --effort FOLDER  the effort's folder, absolute
      --url URL        a GitHub or GitLab issue link; tracker-read.sh --help says
                       which links count
    Requires:  the effort is open; gh (GitHub) or glab (GitLab) logged in
    Writes:    one issue-<host-and-path>.md in the context draft's docs folder,
               headed with its source; a rerun for the same issue replaces it
    Stdout:    one path, absolute: the issue file
    Exit:
      0  written; a partial copy (cut short, comments not read) is noted in
         the file's header
      1  the tracker read failed or timed out; nothing written
      2  refused, nothing written; the reason is on stderr
      3  not a tracker link: add it with context-add.sh --link instead
    [exit 0]
--- usage errors
$ sh main/tracker-read.sh
    tracker-read.sh: --url missing; try --help
    [exit 2]
$ sh main/tracker-read.sh --url
    tracker-read.sh: --url needs a value; try --help
    [exit 2]
$ sh main/tracker-read.sh --url a --url b
    tracker-read.sh: --url given twice; try --help
    [exit 2]
$ sh main/context-add-issue.sh --effort <F>
    context-add-issue.sh: --url missing; try --help
    [exit 2]
--- the link rule: tracker-read.sh and core's context-add.sh --link give the same verdict
    https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/1        tracker-read: accepted context-add: accepted same
    HTTP://Example.com:8080/a?b=c#d            tracker-read: accepted context-add: accepted same
    https://example.com/a b                    tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    https://example.com/a'b                    tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    https://example.com/$(id)                  tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    https://example.com/a;b                    tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    ftp://example.com/x                        tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    https://example.com/a&b                    tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    https://example.com/`x`                    tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    github.com/cli/cli/issues/1                tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
--- not a tracker link (exit 3)
$ sh main/tracker-read.sh --url https://example.com/page
    tracker-read.sh: not a tracker link: example.com/page
    [exit 3]
$ sh main/tracker-read.sh --url https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/1
    tracker-read.sh: not a tracker link: github.com/cli/cli/pull/1
    [exit 3]
$ sh main/tracker-read.sh --url https://github.com/cli/cli/-/issues/1
    tracker-read.sh: not a tracker link: github.com/cli/cli/-/issues/1
    [exit 3]
$ sh main/tracker-read.sh --url https://gitlab.example.com:8443/g/p/-/issues/1
    tracker-read.sh: not a tracker link: gitlab.example.com:8443/g/p/-/issues/1
    [exit 3]
