--- GitHub: a long issue is cut at 500 lines
$ sh main/tracker-read.sh --url https://github.com/golang/go/issues/15292
    # proposal: spec: generic programming facilities
    
    https://github.com/golang/go/issues/15292 · CLOSED · by adg · 2016-04-14T02:33:22Z
    
    This issue proposes that Go should support some form of generic programming.
    It has the Go2 label, since for Go1.x the language is more or less done. 
    
    Accompanying this issue is [a general generics proposal](https://github.com/golang/proposal/blob/master/design/15292-generics.md) by @ianlancetaylor that includes four specific flawed proposals of generic programming mechanisms for Go.
    ... (500 lines on stdout)
    stderr: tracker-read.sh: truncated: showing 500 of 14117 lines
    [exit 0]
--- GitLab: a public issue on gitlab.com with no login: body read, comments not
$ sh main/tracker-read.sh --url https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/issues/1
    # Add functionality to merge merge request
    
    https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/work_items/1 · closed · by profclems · 2020-07-24T23:57:04Z
    
    
    
    ## Comments not read (exit 1: glab: 401 Unauthorized (HTTP 401) )
    ... (7 lines on stdout)
    stderr: 
    [exit 0]
    ## Comments not read (exit 1: glab: 401 Unauthorized (HTTP 401) )
--- GitLab: the copy of a partial issue says so in its header and on stderr
$ sh main/context-add-issue.sh --effort <F> --url https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/issues/1
